  "slug": "tumor-glioblastoma-efcd",
  "summary": "Recent 2026 studies combine bulk and single-cell transcriptomics with WGCNA and ensemble learning to prioritize candidate genes across diverse conditions.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these 20 published studies is a bioinformatic pipeline for nominating candidate molecular markers: public transcriptomic cohorts are combined with co-expression analysis or single-cell profiling, then filtered by machine learning or network-based ranking. Examples span pediatric sepsis, preeclampsia, non-obstructive azoospermia, pulmonary arterial hypertension, and prostate cancer ferroptosis. Several add mechanistic or clinical layers: a 12-gene immune signature with AUC 0.87 for NOA, Mendelian randomization for CKD and keloid, and experimental validation of miR-7-5p/ACTC1 and CD74 in bullous pemphigoid. The novelty lies mainly in the biological axis studied, such as isonicotinylation, copper metabolism, PTM gene sets, or cuproptosis, rather than in the analytic framework. These are hypothesis-generating; the reported associations do not establish causal roles.",
